# A verification finding is fixed, not argued away

A finding raised by an adversarial verification pass, self-review included, is fixed, not argued away. A
blocker or major finding from any independent verifier (any pass but the owning agent's in-context
self-review, one it dispatched included) blocks every change carrying its defect, fail-closed, until
closed. Such a finding closes only by a fix shown by re-verification to remove the named condition, or by
the maintainer's explicit reclassification with a rationale, recorded as the continue-by-default rule
requires a grant to be: a refutation, an argument against the finding, is evidence offered to the
maintainer for that reclassification, never itself a closure, whoever wrote or accepted it; it names each
cause it ruled out with the path and lines read or the command run that ruled it out, and, until closed,
the finding stays open for every other cause of the named condition.
